  "id": "11484_kotokaku",
  "headword": "{事欠|ことか}く",
  "reading": "ことかく",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (godan)",
  "gloss": "to lack, to be short of",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to lack, to be short of, to want for",
      "explanation": "To be in a state of not having enough of something. Most commonly used in the negative form 事欠かない, meaning \"to have no shortage of\" or \"to never lack for.\""
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "11484_kotokaku_ex1",
      "japanese": "{話題|わだい}に{事欠|ことか}かない。",
      "english": "There is no shortage of things to talk about.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "11484_kotokaku_ex2",
      "japanese": "あの{人|ひと}は{問題|もんだい}に{事欠|ことか}かない{人|ひと}だ。",
      "english": "That person is someone who never runs out of problems.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "11484_kotokaku_ex3",
      "japanese": "{食|た}べるものにも{事欠|ことか}くような{生活|せいかつ}をしていた{時代|じだい}があった。",
      "english": "There was a time when people lived lacking even food to eat.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "USAGE:\n{事欠|ことか}く is most frequently used in the negative form {事欠|ことか}かない, meaning \"to have no shortage of\" or \"to never lack.\" The affirmative form {事欠|ことか}く (to lack) is rarer and sounds more literary.\n\nThe pattern ～に{事欠|ことか}かない means \"there is no shortage of ~.\"\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ～に{事欠|ことか}かない: to have no shortage of\n- ～にも{事欠|ことか}く: to lack even ~\n- {話題|わだい}に{事欠|ことか}かない: never at a loss for topics\n- {例|れい}に{事欠|ことか}かない: to have no shortage of examples",
